# @hub-lanes

# ── REPAIR ON PUSH (BH-6963, BH-6542 wave 1) ────────────────────────────────
# Every minute. Reads the push wakes (a push to a repo's default branch) above
# its own wake cursor, reads the paths each push changed once, and runs the
# conductor's mc_rebase at once on every open harness PR whose files intersect
# them, under the conductor's PR lock. At most REPAIR_PUSH_BUDGET (default 8)
# rebases a tick; a capped wake stays above the cursor. flock -n dedupes. One
# REPAIR line per decision in logs/repair-on-push.log. Off:
# flags/lane-off-repair-on-push (bin/harness-ctl.sh off repair-on-push).
* * * * * /root/harness/bin/hub-lease.sh check && /root/harness/bin/repair-on-push.sh >> /root/harness/logs/repair-on-push-cron.log 2>&1
